Z||000000||JohnF||12-13-2001||11:01 AM||||I posted about the time of the 10:34 glitch.  If this is a double post, I apologize.<P>Question is:  On my '88 notchback, I have a 3-wire harness in a connector designed for 4 wires that is plugged in to a connector near the right deck lid hinge.  I have no electrical components in this deck.  No trunk light, no AJAR light, no decklid release.<P>I have had this car since new.  The AJAR light works properly with the front hood and each door. <P>Now, what is this harness?  Can I use it?  Do I need it?  Can I easily add any of the niceties I mention above?<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1578096&a=12001107&p=57211671&Sequence=0"> <BR>You can have all the SPEED you can afford!||||reg||5
Z||000001||FieroJoe||12-13-2001||01:27 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by JohnF:<BR><B>I posted about the time of the 10:34 glitch.  If this is a double post, I apologize.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Go back to my magic topic and read what I posted!  <B>This is the topic I wanted to reply to!</B><P>Very interesting!  So it blew out your topic and replaced it with the wierdo one.  COOL!<P>Hehe, anyways, the three wires you have in your decklid are for the switch to control the trunk light and the AJAR light.  If you do not have a small black switch bolted on to your decklid latch, then your wires are just hanging around up there.  The 4th wire that is not used in the other side of the connector is for the +12V feed to fire the release soleniod.  You should not have anything to worry about if you have neither of these options.  I do find it odd though that the car wouldnt be wired up to the AJAR light.  Double check to make sure that your switch hadnt broken off and then the wires shoved into the decklid or something...I still think that if you didnt get a trunk light your ajar light will still work, so you may be missing the little black switch on the latch mechanism<P><p>[This message has been edited by FieroJoe (edited 12-13-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||JohnF||12-13-2001||02:45 PM||||Thanks for the response and help.  <P>Now, since a new decklid was installed when the car was about a year old due to a drunk taking it out & the repairing Pontiac mechanic may not have re-installed the switch, has anyone got the switch I need or a p/n (source) for that switch?<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1578096&a=12001107&p=57211671&Sequence=0"> <BR>You can have all the SPEED you can afford!||||reg||10
